843:
(a) Scope. The provisions of this section shall apply to all businesses which engage in any of the following operations within the unincorporated areas of the county:
(1) The storage of hazardous wastes;
(2) The treatment of hazardous wastes;
(3) The transportation of hazardous wastes;
(4) The disposal of hazardous wastes.
(b) Definition. As used herein, the term "hazardous wastes" shall apply to all those substances controlled by the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act of 1976, 42 USC 6901 et seq., as amended; Toxic Substances Control Act, 15 USC 2601 et seq., as amended; and the Georgia Hazardous Waste Management Act, O.C.G.A. § 12-8-60 et seq.
(c) License. Each business which engages in the operations described in subsection (a) of this section shall apply for and receive, prior to operation, a county hazardous waste license. Such license shall be subject to renewal each January 1 and shall be in addition to any other license required by this Code. A license fee of $25.00 shall be assessed and collected prior to the issuance of any such license. A county hazardous waste license shall be issued upon proper documentation of all necessary business licenses and all certificates or permits as may be required by state or federal law.
(d) Notice. At least 24 hours prior to any operation described in subsection (a) of this section, each licensee shall provide the office of the clerk of the board of commissioners and the sheriff's department the following information:
(1) Notice of the intended operation and the nature, time and place thereof;
(2) The names of all personnel to be in charge of the operation and on site during the operation; and
(3) If any transportation of hazardous wastes is involved in the operation, the designated route to be taken and the point of origin and destination. If any information should be changed, proper notice should be given immediately. In the event of an accident of any kind or nature involving the storage, transportation, treatment or disposal of hazardous wastes, whether directly or indirectly, proper notification shall be given immediately. Notice shall also be given upon the conclusion of any such operation.
(e) Intent. It is the sole purpose of this section to provide for the health, safety and general welfare of the citizens of the county. These provisions are not intended in any manner to preempt, override, replace or hinder the application of state or federal law nor to prevent the location or operation of a business merely because such business involves hazardous wastes.
(Code 1983, § 11-2; Code 1992, § 10-27)

